      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "g9c7j0ma32b8asc",
                "text": "Gamma Emission"
              }
            ],
            "id": "vsmsqt2tneftdhd",
            "type": "h1"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": ""
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Gamma emission"
                  }
                ],
                "content": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "A type of radioactive decay in which an excited nucleus releases excess energy in the form of gamma rays, which are high-energy photons. This process does not change the atomic number or mass number of the nucleus but brings the nucleus to a lower energy state. Gamma emission often accompanies other forms of decay, such as alpha or beta decay."
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "2891557612",
                    "type": "p"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "1566009642",
                "trigger": "hover",
                "type": "popup"
              },
              {
                "text": " ("
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": ""
                  }
                ],
                "legacyBlockRendered": false,
                "src": "\\gamma",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula_inline"
              },
              {
                "text": " emission) is observed when a nuclide is formed in an excited state and then decays to its ground state with the emission of a "
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": ""
                  }
                ],
                "legacyBlockRendered": false,
                "src": "\\gamma",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula_inline"
              },
              {
                "text": " ray, a quantum of high-energy electromagnetic radiation. An asterisk often indicates the presence of a nucleus in an excited state (*). Cobalt-60 emits "
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": ""
                  }
                ],
                "legacyBlockRendered": false,
                "src": "\\gamma",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula_inline"
              },
              {
                "text": " radiation and is used in many applications, including cancer treatment:"
              }
            ],
            "id": "g5o1iul2pq27ls0",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "i8c4zan67fzs83a",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "gmd0jgodaotb56j",
            "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
            "src": "{}_{27}^{60}\\mathrm{Co}^\\ast\\;\\rightarrow\\;{}_0^0\\mathrm\\gamma\\;+\\;{}_{27}^{60}\\mathrm{Co}",
            "subtype": "latex",
            "type": "formula"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "There is no change in mass number or atomic number during the emission of a "
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": ""
                  }
                ],
                "legacyBlockRendered": false,
                "src": "\\gamma",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula_inline"
              },
              {
                "text": " ray unless the "
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": ""
                  }
                ],
                "legacyBlockRendered": false,
                "src": "\\gamma",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula_inline"
              },
              {
                "text": " emission accompanies one of the other decay modes."
              }
            ],
            "id": "duzmf5hx9at29ck",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "przit37cpaa46jd",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "xm5fuhps4kqhsms",
            "src": "https://d2xvti2irp4c7t.cloudfront.net/media/11/112ef3879b88ef327793a12e23b0c452/gamma_decay2.PNG",
            "type": "img",
            "width": 550
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": ""
              }
            ],
            "id": "2140834490",
            "type": "p"
          }
        ],
